  "description": "Open-source .NET port of Google Tink's AES-256-GCM-HKDF Streaming AEAD (1 MB segments).\n      Fully interoperable with Google Tink (Java, C++, Go, Python) wire format.\n      Encrypt/decrypt multi-gigabyte streams and files without loading them into memory.\n      \n      Features:\n      - Tink wire-format compatible (AES256-GCM-HKDF-1MB)\n      - Streaming — encrypt/decrypt multi-GB files without buffering\n      - Three API styles: static convenience, lazy streams, simplified TinkCrypto facade\n      - Associated Data (AAD) authentication\n      - Multi-target: netstandard2.0 (.NET Framework 4.8+) and net6.0+\n      - Zero native dependencies on modern .NET; Portable.BouncyCastle fallback on netstandard2.0\n      - IAsyncDisposable support on .NET 6+\n      - HKDF-SHA256 key derivation, constant-time key zeroing, hardened against key leakage",
  "id": "TinkStreamingAead",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-16T14:44:32.083Z",
